      bearCase: "The bear case centers on the potential for overly stringent or ambiguous SEC regulations to stifle innovation, impose crippling compliance costs, and deter institutional participation. Technical failures in cross-chain bridges could erode trust and lead to substantial financial losses. Furthermore, concerns over centralization in networks like Zcash could deter privacy-conscious users, while broader macroeconomic downturns could exacerbate market volatility, leading to significant price corrections across the crypto landscape.",
